  "summary": "The study used delaminated Ti3C2Tx prepared by LiF/HCl selective etching of Ti3AlC2 and concentrated with superabsorbent-polymer beads into an additive-free water-based ink. Nine distinct fabricated electrode/device variants are identifiable: four layer-count variants on glass (MSC-1, -2, -5, and -10), four corresponding flexible polymer-substrate variants (MSCF-1, -2, -5, and -10), and a paper-substrate MSC. The headline electrode is MSC-10, which used ten printed layers, had a dried thickness of about 75 \u03bcm, and delivered 1035 mF cm\u22122 at 2 mV s\u22121. Numerical capacitances for the polymer and paper devices, numerical loadings, BET/porosity data, pore sizes, d-spacings, and volumetric or gravimetric capacitances were not provided in the supplied article text."
